cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the Compute Ledger, please cite it as below, with the version you used."
type: dataset
title: "Compute Ledger: public records on the physical, social and economic footprint of AI compute"
authors:
  - name: "Compute Ledger contributors"
version: "1.0.0"
license:
  - CC-BY-4.0
  - MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/kn0wledgebfre3-sys/compute-ledger"
url: "https://kn0wledgebfre3-sys.github.io/compute-ledger/"
abstract: >-
  A public, evidence-based ledger of AI compute's physical, social and economic
  footprint, site by site, built only from public documents. Records (regulators,
  courts, grid operators, statistics offices, auditors, registries, customs) are
  kept apart from claims (what companies and governments say). It holds a registry
  of sourced entries; one validated table of figures with units, periods and the
  basis of each; a register of sites with coordinates where a document gives
  them; a table of documented supply links from mine to site; metered electricity,
  water and fuel from regulators; and the pipeline that rebuilds every output from
  its sources. Data and text are CC BY 4.0; code is MIT.
keywords:
  - datacenters
  - AI compute
  - electricity
  - emissions
  - water
  - air permits
  - public records
  - supply chain
  - semiconductors
